  "notes": "A compound of {遊|ゆう} (play, leisure) and ⟦{歩|ほ}→〜歩：00108_ho⟧ (walk). Most commonly encountered as part of the compound ⟦{遊歩道|ゆうほどう}→遊歩道：23484_yuuhodou⟧ (promenade, walking path/trail), which refers to paved or maintained paths designed for leisurely walking in parks, along riversides, or through scenic areas.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{遊歩道|ゆうほどう}→遊歩道：23484_yuuhodou⟧: promenade, walking trail (the most common compound)\n- {遊歩|ゆうほ}⟦コース→コース：10864_koosu⟧: walking course, strolling route\n- ⟦{森林|しんりん}→森林：01441_shinrin⟧⟦{遊歩道|ゆうほどう}→遊歩道：23484_yuuhodou⟧: forest walking trail\n- ⟦{海岸|かいがん}→海岸：00852_kaigan⟧⟦{遊歩道|ゆうほどう}→遊歩道：23484_yuuhodou⟧: seaside promenade\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{散歩|さんぽ}→散歩：02885_sanpo⟧: walk, stroll — the everyday word for taking a walk; more common in daily conversation\n- ⟦{散策|さんさく}→散策：07618_sansaku⟧: strolling, rambling — slightly more literary, often used for exploring an area on foot\n- {逍遥|しょうよう}: leisurely walk — literary/archaic, rarely used in modern conversation",
